node_modules/
dist/
.turbo/
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Anchored to the repo root: a top-level local-data dir (sqlite files, dumps).
# Unanchored `data/` also matched `apps/server/src/routes/data/` — the CRUD
# route source — and silently kept it out of version control.
/data/
# The same directory when the server is run from its own package, which is what
# every self-host doc and every local smoke test actually does. Anchored for the
# reason above. It holds `adminium.json` — the AES-256-GCM-encrypted meta DSN
# (07 §7.2) — and `meta.db`, so this is about not committing a credential, not
# just tidiness.
/apps/server/data/
# Local-only example databases + their generator toolkit. Schema + seed SQL
# for demo projects (imported into Adminium / Neon / Supabase / PlanetScale) —
# scratch material, never part of the shipped product.
/sample-databases/
# The dashboard build copied into the published package at prepack
# (apps/server/scripts/bundle-dashboard.mjs) — generated, never committed.
/apps/server/dashboard/
# The LLM allow-lists snapshotted into the published package at prepack
# (apps/server/scripts/bundle-allowlists.mjs) — derived from the @adminium/widgets
# registries at build time, so committing it would be a second copy free to rot.
/apps/server/vocabulary/
# Astro's generated type/content cache for @adminium/docs. Regenerated by
# `astro check`/`astro build`; committing it produces churn on every build.
/apps/docs/.astro/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
scripts/release/out/
# Business/design working material — kept locally for reference but never
# committed (and scrubbed from git history). The product workplan and the
# design comps are internal-only, not part of the shipped source.
/workplan/
/designs/
# tsc's incremental cache. Written next to the config by every `--noEmit`
# typecheck (the `tsconfig.json` of each package), so it appears wherever a
# package is typechecked and never belongs in a commit.
*.tsbuildinfo
# Local launch configurations. The working copy carries live sandbox
# credentials (hosted-Postgres DSNs, ADMINIUM_SECRET values) that must never
# reach a public repo; untracked deliberately — see 31 §12.7a.
/.claude/launch.json
